{"kind": "report", "step": 14, "ts": "2026-11-19T15:23:36.555451+00:00", "data": {"category": "dns", "host": "gw.lan", "component": "dns_resolver_config", "cause": "The unbound resolver on gw.lan applies DNS rebinding protection (private-address: 10.0.0.0/8), so it drops the legitimate answer for local names like nas.lan (10.20.0.50) that it forwards to dns1.lan, returning NOERROR with no records; clients whose lookup lands on gw.lan get ENOTFOUND, while internet names are unaffected because they resolve to public addresses.", "evidence": ["dig @10.20.0.3 nas.lan on mon.lan returns 'nas.lan. 10 IN A 10.20.0.50' (NOERROR, ANSWER: 1)", "dig @10.20.0.1 nas.lan on mon.lan returns status NOERROR but ANSWER: 0 \u2014 an empty answer, not a refusal or NXDOMAIN", "drill nas.lan @127.0.0.1 on gw.lan also returns ANSWER: 0, while drill nas.lan @10.20.0.3 from gw.lan returns the A record \u2014 so gw's own resolver empties what dns1 answers", "/var/unbound/unbound.conf on gw.lan contains 'private-address: 10.0.0.0/8' and 'private-address: 127.0.0.0/8' (commented as DNS rebinding protection) plus a forward-zone for 'lan.' to 10.20.0.3 with no private-domain exception", "The record is served with TTL 10, so cached entries expire almost immediately and clients re-query constantly, hitting the filtered path intermittently; each alert clears when a retry lands on dns1.lan"], "action": "change_config", "recommendation": "On gw.lan, stop treating the forwarded internal zone as rebinding: keep the private-address lines for the public view but add 'private-domain: \"lan.\"' (or remove the private-address entries covering the forwarded lan. zone) in /var/unbound/unbound.conf, then reload unbound. Consider raising the very short 10s TTL on dns1.lan for stable names like nas.lan so clients don't re-query so often. No client changes are needed, though listing only dns1.lan would also mask the symptom.", "detail": "unbound private-address rebinding protection discards forwarded .lan answers", "contributing": {"host": "mon.lan", "component": "client_config"}}}
